    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 53,
        "text": "Hi, Ben. You look busy. What are you working on?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "cba63cdb3abcf10df9248ee70a090fb6724a0e679164251a646b91eea113653d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 59,
        "sourceEnd": 209,
        "text": "Oh, hi Mia. I’m preparing a report for my environmental science class. It’s about the campus recycling program. But I’m a bit confused about the data.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3a2a2fc4f79ec0715504370d38b1567e4fd8cbf18f832f1ca24bac9219a4baf6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 215,
        "sourceEnd": 242,
        "text": "Really? What’s the problem?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "48bee8f65fb3330e54f1ea047f622528dd4d02f6a1358f1daec09b65a46c941d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 248,
        "sourceEnd": 394,
        "text": "Well, the recycling bins were placed in all buildings last year, but the amount of recycled paper hasn’t increased much. I thought it would go up.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d7d24dcc20088697a62f447a1967866137eca3d0441bf9bc334226dcbe3b6758",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 400,
        "sourceEnd": 520,
        "text": "Hmm, maybe people are not using them correctly. I saw a sign saying that plastic bags are not allowed in the paper bins.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "ca3cf8bcf6a1a74545946e0dae7474aa76f6ee06faa20a74d6caed01904bf4ca",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 526,
        "sourceEnd": 650,
        "text": "Right, but that sign was put up only last month. Before that, many people threw plastic bags into the paper bins by mistake.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "4db303e189b34d65b4553cb8189c039c487a10afcb8e87980b91072bf57264a8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 656,
        "sourceEnd": 722,
        "text": "So the contamination was caused by the lack of clear instructions?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "eb6d804ee10eb9f8c690a1187e89e0ed25fc8f02e49a40dfffcc4cdc41339ea5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 728,
        "sourceEnd": 876,
        "text": "Exactly. The recycling company said that contaminated paper cannot be processed, so it’s sent to the landfill. That’s why the recycling rate is low.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2cba1c7b9ff20176aa0f48daa98d728dd9a58c9aae9f7d5d54b9bf0406f2bdbe",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 882,
        "sourceEnd": 928,
        "text": "That makes sense. So what are you going to do?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "147d2a04c8566b26370352bd30c5468f1849229295643d2b113f9852e876d19f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 934,
        "sourceEnd": 1091,
        "text": "I’m going to recommend more workshops for students. Also, I’m reading some articles about recycling behavior. But I find academic articles difficult to read.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "c03c2e2a9b98a8904f6f7e1506680f752101b61456e533295b6874a1278c1fc6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1097,
        "sourceEnd": 1262,
        "text": "Me too. I learned a strategy called “reading for gist” – you read the title, abstract, and conclusion first to get the main idea, then you look for specific details.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a83404968d2290aa9866dd5d244499e0649e2c7f1c841632bd2144983c0d6280",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1268,
        "sourceEnd": 1324,
        "text": "That sounds helpful. So I don’t need to read every word?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "462ed5a5a50a3bbdbcf1fc1f48c13ef22c1ad296bf9e998cb3edec7d368621c5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1330,
        "sourceEnd": 1475,
        "text": "No, especially for long articles. You can also look for signal words like “because”, “therefore”, “as a result” to understand causes and effects.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "69b36141a933821f72a46dacb6c050abd99eaaa130d2158e2f7f0e25478303a5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1481,
        "sourceEnd": 1518,
        "text": "Good tip. I’ll try that. Thanks, Mia!",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "70ff326817fda115666dec6f9985259a03939802f42379be4eb79c16332ef67c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1524,
        "sourceEnd": 1567,
        "text": "You’re welcome. Good luck with your report!",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "fe7e3b7c939c6b4bdc0373b01716a1a185bc7b70d150368b5794ffe3fb432448",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
